       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for sertraline in adults, which is 200 mg/day. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit. At this dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI effects and seizures.\n\nCould you check which of these applies?\n\n- **Typo or unit error:** The intended dose may be 40 mg or 100 mg. Usual dosing is 50\u2013200 mg once daily. Tell me the dose and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Dose is intentional:** If you mean to go above the labeled maximum, tell me the indication and that you've confirmed it. I can enter it with a note, for example \"Dose exceeds labeled max, confirmed by prescriber.\" I'd suggest running it by pharmacy too.\n- **Other serotonergic drugs:** If the patient is on other serotonergic drugs, such as linezolid, tramadol, triptans or MAOIs, that raises the risk further.\n\nHow would you like to proceed?"
